SUMMARY:Happy Halloween Costume Swap
DTSTART;TZID=America/New_York:20261003T090000
DTEND;TZID=America/New_York:20261003T120000
UID:f8832409d590f4eeec6c084553f56508@calendar.lancasterlibraries.org
DESCRIPTION:Arts & Crafts\, Babies\, Toddlers\, Children\, Tweens\n\nJoin 
 us for our Library Costume Swap!Bring in a clean\, gently used costume (bi
 rth through tween sizes) and trade it for something “new-to-you.” This
  fun community event is a wonderful way to share\, connect\, and celebrate
  together while giving costumes a second life. Swapping not only helps fam
 ilies save money\, but it’s also a great way to support the environment 
 by keeping costumes out of the landfill. Come be part of this exciting new
  tradition!Bring a Costume to SwapCostumes for birth through youth size 14
  (tween size) only.Costumes must be clean\, gently used\, and in good cond
 ition (no rips\, stains\, pet hair\, or missing pieces).Accessories like h
 ats\, masks\, wands\, or capes are welcome if safe and complete. (No makeu
 p\, wigs\, or undergarments).Drop-Off & TicketsCostumes must be dropped of
 f between 9:00–9:30 am.For each accepted costume\, you’ll receive one 
 swap ticket.Tickets can be used starting at 10:00 am to “shop” for a n
 ew costume.Fair SwappingOne ticket = one costume.Families may only take as
  many costumes as they bring.At 11:30 am\, if costumes remain\, anyone (in
 cluding those who did not drop off a costume) may select extras. While sup
 plies last.Condition & FitAll costumes are offered “as is.” The librar
 y is not responsible for sizing\, safety\, or condition.LeftoversAny lefto
 ver costumes at noon will be donated to local charities.
LOCATION:Manheim Township\, MTP Morgan Center BC
URL:https://calendar.lancasterlibraries.org/event/happy-halloween-costume-
 swap-167861
X-SOURCE:Lancaster Libraries
END:VEVENT
