SUMMARY:What Teeth Tell Us
DTSTART;TZID=America/New_York:20261003T110000
DTEND;TZID=America/New_York:20261003T120000
UID:8c784c7edfc11625cbd2ef52bfd0c166@calendar.lancasterlibraries.org
DESCRIPTION:Presentation\, Everyone\n\nWhat big teeth you have!Most dinosa
 urs are known for their incredible teeth! By studying their teeth alone\, 
 scientists can decide what each type ate for dinner whether it be meat\, p
 lants\, or a little bit of everything. In modern times we still use the te
 eth in animals’ skulls to learn a lot about them. Join a Naturalist from
  Lancaster County's Department of Parks & Recreation to discover the scien
 ce of teeth and what they can tell us. Then\, try your hand at identifying
  skulls to figure out what certain mystery animals like to have for dinner
 . All ages · Walk-ins welcome
LOCATION:Lancaster\, LPL Community Room
URL:https://calendar.lancasterlibraries.org/event/what-teeth-tell-us-16635
 6
X-SOURCE:Lancaster Libraries
END:VEVENT
