X-SOURCE-URLS:{"Figlancaster": "https://figlancaster.com/event/screen-printing-social-justice-posters-workshop-at-pcad/"}
X-SOURCE-ID:figlancaster
X-SOURCE:Fig Lancaster
DTSTART;TZID=America/New_York:20261007T180000
DTEND;TZID=America/New_York:20261007T210000
DTSTAMP:20261002T182019Z
CREATED:20260930T134025Z
LAST-MODIFIED:20261002T182019Z
UID:10015057-1791396000-1791406800@figlancaster.com
SUMMARY:Screen Printing Social Justice Posters Workshop at PCA&D
DESCRIPTION:Printed media has a long history of being used as a tool in activism and social justice movements. Printmaking allows one to make multiple copies of their artwork\, ideas\, and beliefs and distribute them to friends\, on the street\, and anywhere else they can think of. In this class\, students will create a poster design for a subject they feel passionate about and bring it to life as a screen printed poster. This class will cover a brief history of social justice posters\, the process of creating a screen\, and screenprinting techniques. At the end of the class\, students are free to trade copies of their posters with each other. All supplies will be provided. Just bring your ideas! \n            \n        \n                \n            \n                \n                \n    Register Now
URL:https://figlancaster.com/event/screen-printing-social-justice-posters-workshop-at-pcad/
LOCATION:Pennsylvania College of Art & Design – Center for Creative Exploration\, 204 North Prince Street\, Lancaster\, Pennsylvania\, 17603\, United States
CATEGORIES:Education & Classes
