DTSTART;TZID=America/New_York:20261013T130000
DTEND;TZID=America/New_York:20261013T140000
UID:2ba31dc09b0a45fa6c93a4e92ded290e@calendar.lancasterlibraries.org
DESCRIPTION:Community\, Discussion\, Health & Wellness\, Presentation\, Ch
 ildren\, Tweens\, Teens\, Adults\, Seniors\, Everyone\n\nJoin us for a fas
 cinating\, hands-on science adventure led by the experts from Lancaster Co
 unty Parks!As nocturnal hunters\, owls seem to intrigue people more than a
 ny other birds. Their predatory nature\, unique adaptations\, and phenomen
 al senses are fascinating. Participants will learn about our local owls\, 
 their sounds\, adaptations\, and preferred habitats. We will end the progr
 am with an owl pellet dissection. What to Expect:Local Species: Learn abou
 t native owl species in Pennsylvania.Adaptations: Discover how these noctu
 rnal hunters survive and thrive.Tactile Station: Get a hands-on look at re
 al owl feathers\, talons\, and skulls.Pellet Dissection: Roll up your slee
 ves and dissect an owl pellet to uncover what they eat!Space is limited\, 
 and pre-registration is required! Reserve your spot today!
LOCATION:Manheim Community\, MAN Kreider Cultural Center
URL:https://calendar.lancasterlibraries.org/event/owl-pellet-disection-202
 654
