X-SOURCE-ID:lancaster_libraries
SUMMARY:Screening of The Golem: How He Came Into the World (1920 Silent Fi
 lm)
DTSTART;TZID=America/New_York:20261015T180000
DTEND;TZID=America/New_York:20261015T193000
UID:f2fc6f9e8c42f39eef2cf8da3c71b916@calendar.lancasterlibraries.org
DESCRIPTION:Movie & Film\, Adults\, Seniors\n\nAdults 18+Join us for a fre
 e screening of the 1920 silent film\, The Golem: How He Came Into the Worl
 d. The film is part of our grant funded programming through the Yiddish Bo
 ok Center. Yiddish Book CenterThe Golem: How He Came into the World (Der G
 olem\, wie er in die Welt kam\, 1920) is a German silent horror film direc
 ted by Paul Wegener (with Carl Boese) and co-written by Henrik Galeen\, ba
 sed on Gustav Meyrink’s 1915 novel.  It is considered a leading example 
 of early German Expressionism and is notable for being the only surviving 
 film in a trilogy of golem-themed works by Wegener.The movie runs 1 hour a
 nd 15 minutes. Popcorn and soda will be served.
LOCATION:Lititz\, LTZ Community Room
URL:https://calendar.lancasterlibraries.org/event/screening-golem-how-he-c
 ame-world-1920-silent-film-195564
