UID:38650-1792170000-1792182600@apostlesucc.org
SUMMARY:Mocktails & Meaning™: Lightworkers Documentary
DESCRIPTION:As the 2026 midterm elections approach\, Lightworkers invites us to consider the role each of us can play in strengthening our communities and democracy. On Friday\, October 16th\, this special Mocktails & Meaning™ gathering will feature a free screening of Lightworkers\, a documentary directed by Bobby Roth that shares personal stories from people responding to social\, political\, and environmental challenges. The film explores individual choices\, collective responsibility\, and the many ways people can contribute to a more just and compassionate world. A light dinner will be served from 5–6 PM\, followed by the documentary at 6 PM and a Q&A with director Bobby Roth afterward. Come watch\, reflect\, and consider the film’s central question: What can we do?
URL:https://apostlesucc.org/event/mocktails-meaning-lightworkers-documentary/
LOCATION:Church of the Apostles UCC\, 1850 Marietta Ave\, Lancaster\, PA\, 17603\, United States
ATTACH;FMTTYPE=image/jpeg:https://apostlesucc.org/wp-content/uploads/2026/09/Mocktails-Meaning-Flyer-Banner-Landscape-1-scaled.jpg
END:VEVENT
