UID:48ee7cc422ac9b523b974e5bf46bc095@calendar.lancasterlibraries.org
DESCRIPTION:Arts & Crafts\, Children\, Tweens\n\nAges 6-12\, children unde
 r 8 should have responsible caregiver present. Some sessions will be held 
 outside if weather permits.Our main program room is named for Charles X. C
 arlson\, the notable local artist. And what more fitting purpose than to u
 se it to inspire a new generation of artists! Carlson Kids is a new grant-
 funded program that brings together a local art teacher\, some aspiring te
 en coaches\, and young future artists!  Students will do art activities in
  similar styles to Charlie Carlson's work\, which includes watercolor\, co
 llage\, cartooning\, and some experimental projects. This program will be 
 offered on one Thursday afternoon and one Saturday afternoon per month. Yo
 u may register for any sessions you wish\, attendance at all sessions is n
 ot mandatory. We gratefully acknowledge the C. X. Carlson Cultural Trust F
 und for their generosity in providing this program to our community.
LOCATION:Quarryville\, QVL C.X. Carlson Cultural Room
