BEGIN:VEVENT
X-SOURCE-URLS:{"Lancaster Libraries": "https://calendar.lancasterlibraries.org/event/tabletop-rpgs-adults-165130"}
X-SOURCE-ID:lancaster_libraries
SUMMARY:Tabletop RPGs for Adults
DTSTART;TZID=America/New_York:20261021T170000
DTEND;TZID=America/New_York:20261021T200000
UID:01851883e827d0a6a2249aee4cb06c64@calendar.lancasterlibraries.org
DESCRIPTION:Gaming\, Adults\n\nJoin local GM Matt as he runs a variety of 
 Tabletop Role Playing Games that rotate each month. No experience in any s
 ystem is required and anyone interested in dipping their toes into the TTR
 PG world are welcomed and encouraged to join in on the fun!This month's ga
 me is: DaggerheartThe town of Cadence is one steeped in superstition. It w
 as built over a century ago when a large copper mine was established nearb
 y promising wealth and prosperity. However\, the mine was located within t
 he soft grounds of a swamp leading to poor living conditions for the miner
 s on shift\, frequent cave-ins\, hazardous gasses\, and a variety of other
  fatal accidents. Disregarding the cries from the public to shut the mine 
 down the owner of the copper mine\, Liviett Truce kept her operation going
  for nearly 30 years with little care of her employed miners.One day rumor
 s of a creature stalking the mining camps in the swamp made their way back
  to Cadence. Miners would go missing\, claw marks raked through the canvas
  of their tents\, trails of blood leading out into the murky waters of the
  swamp. The town erupted in a panic and the workers left the camps on stri
 ke. Liviett wanted to put an end to the strike swiftly and as frugally as 
 possible so she decided to go visit the now emptied mining camps to prove 
 no such creature exists. Liviett Truce never returned and the mine was aba
 ndoned.Today\, 85 years later\, rumors of a creature in the swamp making p
 eople disappear have begun circulating again within the streets of Cadence
 . A large sum of gold has been offered on local bulletins to anyone who ca
 n procure the head of this creature or proof of its non-existence. The bul
 letin is sponsored by Cosdum Truce\, grandson of Liviett. Registration is 
 required. This group is for adults only.
LOCATION:Manheim Township\, MTP Study Room #119
URL:https://calendar.lancasterlibraries.org/event/tabletop-rpgs-adults-165
 130
X-SOURCE:Lancaster Libraries
END:VEVENT
