DESCRIPTION:Storytime\, Toddlers\, Children\n\nBring the whole family to t
 he library for a delightful storytime experience! Perfect for children age
 s 0-12\, this program features engaging stories\, lively songs\, and fun a
 ctivities designed to spark a love of reading and learning. This is a wond
 erful opportunity for families to bond\, build literacy skills\, and creat
 e lasting memories together!Adults attending with their child(ren) do NOT 
 need to register. Please add any additional registrants to your registrati
 on if more than one child that will be participating in the program.Regist
 ration will open at 9:00AM on Wednesday\, October 28th for Manheim Townshi
 p and East Lampeter residents and on Friday\, October 30th for residents o
 f other municipalities.Storytime PoliciesNo Show – Patrons failing to ca
 ncel their registration for more than 2 library programs in a month will b
 e restricted from registering for future programs for a period of one mont
 h’s time. Please cancel your registrations at least 2 hours prior to the
  start of the program to allow for those on the waiting list to be notifie
 d of their change in registration status.Late Arrivals – Please arrive 1
 0 minutes prior to the start of the program to allow for parking and other
  circumstances. The program will begin promptly at the designated time. At
  this time\, your spot will be forfeited to those on the wait list who wil
 l be granted entry. If spots remain\, registrants may be allowed into the 
 program. However\, registrants will not be permitted to enter the program 
 5 minutes past the start time.Accompanying Adults – This program is for 
 adults and children to enjoy together. Please plan to attend and be engage
 d with your child. Drop offs will not be permitted.Cancellations- Please c
 heck your email prior to departing to verify that the program has not been
  cancelled.
